{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfs5sx4LgujhZErPWRFzS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The cause was mutable default arguments in `inv/warehouse.py`. The test now passes (1 passed), and it's the only test in the repo.\n\n- **`Warehouse.__init__`:** `stock={}` and `history=[]` were created once at function definition, so every `Warehouse` built without those arguments shared the same dict and list. That is why a second warehouse showed the first one's stock, and why `restock` on one changed another. They now default to `None` and each instance gets its own fresh `{}` and `[]`.\n- **`restock`:** the `tags=[]` default had the same problem. The list went straight into each new `Item`, so items would have shared one tags list. It now defaults to `None`, and each `Item` gets its own copy of the tags.\n\nI didn't touch the test. I haven't committed anything."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7146,"cache_read_input_tokens":37130,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7146},"output_tokens":261,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a1ba22a9-a45f-4c2f-a7ce-fbc142ee47b3","uuid":"51200e44-81b8-482a-804c-5b74ae0e8f8d","timestamp":"2026-10-09T17:49:09.173Z","request_id":"req_011Cfs5swoTvSzh9EnbQWC78"}
